#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:8
msgid "docker interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The `docker` interface allows client access to the Docker socket. Use this "
"interface when you want to interact with the Docker daemon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"Due to the nature of containers, the permissions granted to the [Docker snap]"
"(https://snapcraft.io/docker) allow it to bypass elements of the _snapd_ "
"security sandbox. This is acceptable because the Docker snap publisher is "
"trusted and because applications running inside such containers are further "
"isolated with the sandbox built by Docker itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"While anyone can rebuild the [Docker snap from source](https://github.com/"
"docker-snap/docker-snap), not everyone is immediately trusted with the "
"privileged interfaces it requires to function. This interface can be used "
"instead to permit such access by allowing snapped applications to "
"communicate with the Docker daemon socket on the Docker snap. This enables "
"anyone to create and publish a snap that requires Docker without requiring "
"the same privileged interfaces required by the Docker snap itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:18
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Interface management <how-to-guides-work-with-snaps-connect-"
"interfaces>` and {ref}`Supported interfaces <ref-index_interfaces>` for "
"further details on how interfaces are used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:23
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:25
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`**: yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:25
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:29
msgid ""
"The `docker` slot is {ref}`unsupported for parallel instances <interfaces-"
"parallel-installs-unsupported>`. The slot owns a unique system-wide resource "
"that instances would conflict over."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:32
msgid ""
"For distribution via the [Snap store ](https://snapcraft.io/store), "
"consumers of this interface require an approved {ref}`snap declaration "
"<interfaces-process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:34
msgid "Example implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:36
msgid ""
"The source code for a complete example snap that communicates with the "
"Docker snap can be found here: [github.com/zyga/hello-docker](https://"
"github.com/zyga/hello-docker)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:38
msgid "The following is an excerpt from the above snap's snapcraft.yaml:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:40
msgid ""
"base: core22\n"
"confinement: strict\n"
"apps:\n"
"  hello-docker:\n"
"    command: usr/bin/hello-docker\n"
"    environment:\n"
"      PATH: $SNAP/docker-snap/bin:$PATH\n"
"    plugs:\n"
"      - docker\n"
"      - docker-executables\n"
"plugs:\n"
"  docker:\n"
"    label: Access to the docker communication socket\n"
"  docker-executables:\n"
"    label: Access to the docker command-line utilities\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: docker-executables\n"
"    target: $SNAP/docker-snap\n"
"    default-provider: docker\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:62
msgid ""
"This snapcraft.yaml will build a {ref}`strictly confined <explanation-"
"security-snap-confinement>` snap package which is portable across "
"environments and works equally on IoT-centric Ubuntu Core as well as on most "
"commonly used desktop and server distributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:64
msgid ""
"The snap has one apps definition which contains the `hello-docker` "
"application. This application uses two snap interface plugs, one called "
"_docker_ and the other called _docker-executables_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:66
msgid ""
"The plugs for both are defined in more detail in the `plugs:` section. In "
"this section, _docker_ refers to this specific interface while _docker-"
"executables_ is an example of a {ref}`content interface <interfaces-content-"
"interface>`. The content interface is further specified to refer to content "
"of type docker-executables. This is important as it has to match what is "
"[provided by the Docker snap](https://github.com/docker-snap/docker-snap/"
"blob/058337577d4172c8919a53a41c38ebe7ee9beab0/snap/snapcraft.yaml#L90C1-"
"L90C22) available in the store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:68
msgid ""
"Plugs of the content interface have the target attribute which defines where "
"the corresponding content is made available. In this case, it is the "
"directory `docker-snap` inside the read-only image of the application snap. "
"It is important that our application snap contains an empty directory with "
"the same name, so that when the Docker snap is installed and the interfaces "
"are connected, we can access the Docker snap's command line tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:70
msgid ""
"The app definition contains an environment variable that directs the "
"application to look for Docker executables in the `$SNAP/docker-snap/bin` "
"sub-directory. This sub-directory will only exist when the content interface "
"is connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:72
msgid ""
"Lastly, the default-provider field tells snapd that if the user does not "
"have any snap with a compatible interface installed, then upon installation "
"of our snap, the docker snap is automatically installed and connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:74
msgid ""
"When the above example snap is built and installed, you can open a shell "
"within the snap's environment with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:77
msgid "snap run --shell hello-docker\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/docker-interface.md:81
msgid ""
"The Docker command line tool, among other Docker-related executables, can be "
"found within `$SNAP/docker-snap/bin`. Since this is within the `$PATH`, "
"Docker can now be used within your own scripts, or for whatever purpose you "
"may require."
msgstr ""
